0,Savosavo language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Savosavo_language,"Savosavo is one of the Central Solomon languages, which are Papuan languages, unlike most of the languages in the vicinity, which are members of the Oceanic branch of the Austronesian language family.",Savosavo,Central Solomons
1,Savosavo | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/svs/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..O8j1_gxTB_NtU2-PjsFN5cy0RFTTkfpMDhnwhZEfT2g,Savosavo is a stable indigenous language of the Solomon Islands. It belongs to the Central Solomons language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,Savosavo,Central Solomons
2,Savosavo - DOBES,https://dobes.mpi.nl/projects/savosavo/,"• The Savosavo archive contains audio and video material, mostly narratives (customary folk stories, procedural texts, stories about historical events and traditional customs), songs, dances, elicited sessions, and recordings during workshops on several topics. •",Savosavo,Central Solomons
3,Savosavo languagea and alphabet,https://www.omniglot.com/writing/savosavo.htm,"Savosavo is a Central Solomons language spoken on Savo Island in the Solomon Islands by about 2,500 people.Savosavo alphabet and pronunciation. This is the Unified orthography.",Savosavo,Central Solomons
4,Savosavo - svs (Central Solomons) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/svs/,"Savosavo – svs is in the Central Solomons family, included in Central Solomons language class.People Groups who primarily speak Savosavo. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.",Savosavo,Central Solomons
